---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { downloads } from '../../config/downloads';
---

<Page
  title="Can't sleep before your period? PMS insomnia explained · Niyora"
  description="Lying awake in the days before your period is common. Here is the science behind PMS insomnia, why sleep gets lighter and the mind races, and what actually helps."
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com/pms/insomnia/"
>
  <section class="s hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">PMS insomnia</div>
    <h1>Can't sleep before your period? PMS insomnia explained</h1>
    <p class="lead">In the days before your period, sleep can turn light and restless. You lie awake, or you wake at 3am with your mind racing. This is a normal hormonal shift changing how your body settles at night, and it eases as the shift passes.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Why sleep gets harder before your period</h2>
    <div class="science">
      <p>Progesterone breaks down into a calming compound, allopregnanolone, that helps you wind down through the GABA system. As progesterone falls before your period, that calming support drops, so sleep gets lighter and harder to hold. Your sleep and wake rhythm can shift in this window too.</p>
      <p>On top of that, a sensitised nervous system stays a little more alert. The same worries that would quiet down any other night keep pulling you back awake. Your hormone levels are normal. The difference is how strongly your system responds to the shift, and some systems feel it more.</p>
      <p>And it has an end date. As the hormonal shift passes, usually once your period starts, sleep settles back to its usual pattern. It shows up with the shift, and it eases with the next one, every cycle.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>What helps when you're lying awake</h2>
    <p class="lead">Niyora is built for the moment you are awake and wired. Three small steps, about a minute, to bring your body down.</p>
    <div class="rrr-grid">
      <div class="rrr-card">
        <div class="rrr-label">Reflect</div>
        <p>Name what is happening. Seeing that the wakefulness is the calming dial turned low for a few nights, not a sign the night is ruined, takes some of the pressure off.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rrr-card">
        <div class="rrr-label">Regulate</div>
        <p>Settle your body in about a minute. A slower breath with a longer exhale shifts your system toward rest. You cannot force sleep, but you can lower the alert that is keeping you from it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rrr-card">
        <div class="rrr-label">Respond</div>
        <p>With your body calmer, you can let the racing thought go instead of chasing it, and give sleep room to return on its own.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Keep reading</h2>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/blog/how-to-sleep-when-your-mind-wont-stop/" class="btn ghost">How to sleep when your mind won't stop</a>
      <a href="/blog/how-to-stop-overthinking-at-night/" class="btn ghost">How to stop overthinking at night</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="s">
    <h2>Not sure the sleepless nights are PMS?</h2>
    <p class="lead">Take the two-minute check and see how your premenstrual week actually hits.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/quiz" class="btn">Take the quiz</a>
      <a href={downloads.appStore} class="btn ghost">Get Niyora</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  /* Page-specific only: the science block and the R/R/R grid. Shared chrome
     (sheet, sections, dividers, type scale, buttons, footer) comes from Page. */
  .science {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 32px 30px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.28);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .science p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.65; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78); margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .science p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .rrr-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 24px auto 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .rrr-card {
    padding: 24px 22px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  }
  .rrr-label {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.9);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .rrr-card p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82); }

  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; margin-top: 28px; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .s { padding: 56px 24px; }
    h1 { font-size: 34px; }
    h2 { font-size: 26px; }
    .rrr-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .science p { font-size: 16px; }
  }
</style>
